@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.1824 = private unnamed_addr constant [698 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for problematic `sys.version_info`-related conditions in stubs.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub files support simple conditionals to test for differences in Python\0Aversions using `sys.version_info`. However, there are a number of common\0Amistakes involving `sys.version_info` comparisons that should be avoided.\0AFor example, comparing against a string can lead to unexpected behavior.\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif sys.version_info[0] == \222\22: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Aimport sys\0A\0Aif sys.version_info[0] == 2: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation: Version and Platform checking](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/directives.html#version-and-platform-checks)\0A", align 1
