@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2006 = private unnamed_addr constant [867 x i8] c"## What it does\0ACheck for `type: ignore` annotations that suppress all type warnings, as\0Aopposed to targeting specific type warnings.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASuppressing all warnings can hide issues in the code.\0A\0ABlanket `type: ignore` annotations are also more difficult to interpret and\0Amaintain, as the annotation does not clarify which warnings are intended\0Ato be suppressed.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom foo import secrets  # type: ignore\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom foo import secrets  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\0A```\0A\0A## References\0AMypy supports a [built-in setting](https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/error_code_list2.html#check-that-type-ignore-include-an-error-code-ignore-without-code)\0Ato enforce that all `type: ignore` annotations include an error code, akin\0Ato enabling this rule:\0A```toml\0A[tool.mypy]\0Aenable_error_code = [\22ignore-without-code\22]\0A```\0A", align 1
