@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2066 = private unnamed_addr constant [470 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `yield from` in async functions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APython doesn't support the use of `yield from` in async functions, and will\0Araise a `SyntaxError` in such cases.\0A\0AInstead, considering refactoring the code to use an `async for` loop instead.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aasync def numbers():\0A    yield from [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aasync def numbers():\0A    async for number in [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]:\0A        yield number\0A```\0A", align 1
