@anon.9a3c7070530f84c5ad699604f23a6f35.2110 = private unnamed_addr constant [564 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the presence of unused variables in unpacked assignments.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA variable that is defined but never used can confuse readers.\0A\0AIf a variable is intentionally defined-but-not-used, it should be\0Aprefixed with an underscore, or some other value that adheres to the\0A[`lint.dummy-variable-rgx`] pattern.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Adef get_pair():\0A    return 1, 2\0A\0A\0Adef foo():\0A    x, y = get_pair()\0A    return x\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Adef foo():\0A    x, _ = get_pair()\0A    return x\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.dummy-variable-rgx`\0A", align 1
